WEBVTT

00:02.520 --> 00:07.190
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

00:07.190 --> 00:11.520
<i>Charging at full speed, straight ahead</i>

00:09.480 --> 00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:11.520 --> 00:13.330
<i>That's how I live</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:29.750
<i>I keep turning them over in my mind</i>

00:29.750 --> 00:32.720
<i>All the things I want to do</i>

00:32.720 --> 00:39.970
<i>Even if I'm told that's not 
what's expected of me</i>

00:39.970 --> 00:43.310
<i>I don't plan on giving them up</i>

00:43.310 --> 00:51.870
<i>Ah, dreams are meant to be big</i>

00:51.870 --> 00:56.840
<i>I'll head where the shining coin points me</i>

00:56.840 --> 01:01.870
<i>And nothing can stop me</i>

01:01.870 --> 01:07.000
<i>I won't back down, I'll face forward</i>

01:07.000 --> 01:12.250
<i>So I can fulfill my dream</i>

01:12.550 --> 01:17.180
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

01:17.180 --> 01:21.560
<i>Wind at my back, giving it my all</i>

01:21.560 --> 01:23.300
<i>That's how I live</i>

01:29.980 --> 01:32.980
The Messenger Goes into Battle

01:33.480 --> 01:36.090
Damn it! It's impossible for us to cross now!

01:36.090 --> 01:38.360
What do we do?! 
The monsters are approaching!

01:44.520 --> 01:45.580
It really isn't working!

01:53.420 --> 01:56.480
They may be monsters, but it looks like 
their brains are still in their heads.

01:56.480 --> 01:58.470
Nice one, Captain!

02:03.430 --> 02:04.520
That being said...

02:04.520 --> 02:06.350
Damn it, there's no end to them!

02:06.350 --> 02:07.870
How are things back there?

02:08.850 --> 02:10.600
Looks like they still can't cross.

02:10.600 --> 02:12.770
So we need to hold the fort 
a little longer, huh?

02:13.180 --> 02:14.110
How much ammo do you have?

02:14.110 --> 02:15.940
Not a whole lot.

02:15.940 --> 02:17.820
Enough to last two or three minutes at most!

02:17.820 --> 02:20.550
<i>If we jumped worlds, 
the two of us would be safe.</i>

02:20.550 --> 02:21.570
<i>But...</i>

02:21.570 --> 02:24.490
<i>We can't just abandon those people!</i>

02:24.490 --> 02:26.910
<i>What now? What do we do?</i>

02:29.930 --> 02:32.790
<i>Jump back to Wolf's Fang 
and ask for reinforcements?</i>

02:32.790 --> 02:36.300
<i>No! It'll take too long to convince them all!</i>

02:36.300 --> 02:40.510
<i>I don't know what weapons we would 
even bring, and we'd need to prepare!</i>

02:42.350 --> 02:44.890
They've brought all their 
little friends along, as well!

02:44.890 --> 02:46.770
What, are they on their way 
to a bargain sale?!

02:48.250 --> 02:51.730
<i>Brought along their friends? Bargain?</i>

02:51.730 --> 02:54.270
1 person = 10% off

02:51.730 --> 02:54.270
5 people = half price

02:51.920 --> 02:54.270
If you bring one person, I'll give you 10% off.

02:54.270 --> 02:57.430
All right, we'll bring them. 
We'll bring the whole guild here!

02:58.490 --> 03:01.320
Then we can get this firestarter, 
a stove, some rations...

03:02.570 --> 03:06.050
Captain! Hold them off here 
for two more minutes!

03:06.800 --> 03:08.010
H-Hey!

03:08.010 --> 03:10.560
Well, I'm used to it by now...

03:10.560 --> 03:13.750
Two minutes, huh? 
She makes it sound so easy!

03:16.000 --> 03:19.670
Jeez, been a while since I've had 
to work so hard for my pay.

03:20.560 --> 03:22.430
In here, there should be...

03:23.680 --> 03:25.800
Found it! And also...

03:25.800 --> 03:28.970
<b>Fireworks Set</b>

03:27.440 --> 03:28.970
That's it!

03:37.150 --> 03:38.260
Damn it!

03:38.260 --> 03:40.880
There's only so much I can do 
with so many of them!

03:41.290 --> 03:43.070
I'm back now!

03:43.230 --> 03:44.810
Did you bring back some weapons?

03:44.810 --> 03:45.920
Please back me up!

03:45.920 --> 03:46.960
H-Hey!

03:50.160 --> 03:51.270
There we go!

03:51.910 --> 03:52.870
Huh?!

03:58.500 --> 04:00.390
Nice one, little lady!

04:00.390 --> 04:01.970
And now, for good measure!

04:02.170 --> 04:04.260
<b>Fountain 
Firework</b>

04:14.060 --> 04:16.690
Hey, now. Talk about overkill...

04:25.490 --> 04:26.990
Who the hell is that?

04:26.990 --> 04:29.910
He might be a monster handler for the enemy...

04:29.910 --> 04:31.360
I see...

04:36.260 --> 04:38.540
Looks like we managed to scrape by here.

04:38.540 --> 04:39.610
Yes!

04:46.520 --> 04:49.140
Hooray! We did it!

04:49.140 --> 04:50.370
You saved us!

04:52.880 --> 04:54.140
Hey!

04:54.960 --> 04:57.980
Looks like that monster handler got away.

04:57.980 --> 04:59.410
Let's leave him be.

04:59.410 --> 05:01.600
I'm sure he won't cause trouble anytime soon.

05:01.600 --> 05:05.570
Got it. I've worked my share 
for this gold coin, then.

05:05.570 --> 05:07.360
Thank you very much.

05:07.360 --> 05:10.070
I believe you about other worlds and monsters.

05:10.070 --> 05:11.490
But the enemy number 20,000.

05:11.490 --> 05:13.580
And they've got resilient monsters, as well.

05:13.890 --> 05:16.380
There are probably even stronger monsters.

05:16.380 --> 05:18.330
Is this too difficult 
a request to ask of you?

05:26.490 --> 05:29.360
You said it pays a minimum 
guarantee of 40,000 gold,

05:29.360 --> 05:31.860
plus additional compensation 
as appropriate, right?

05:31.860 --> 05:32.770
Yes.

05:34.270 --> 05:37.060
Make sure you fork up plenty 
of additional pay, young lady!

05:37.060 --> 05:38.250
Eh?

05:38.250 --> 05:39.880
I couldn't ask for a more worthy foe.

05:39.880 --> 05:40.770
So you mean...

05:41.730 --> 05:45.240
Time for an emergency 
gathering of PMC Wolf's Fang!

06:01.150 --> 06:02.880
They say the Imperial army 
has launched an invasion!

06:02.880 --> 06:03.890
What?!

06:03.890 --> 06:07.030
I heard the king is assembling 
soldiers in the capital!

06:07.030 --> 06:09.340
Will Mitsuha be okay?

06:10.800 --> 06:12.360
Go! Hurry!

06:12.360 --> 06:14.100
Make sure you fill up on gas!

06:15.940 --> 06:18.770
Is this Professor Bishop 
from Harvard University?

06:19.830 --> 06:22.860
Yes, we're the ones who took that photo.

06:23.270 --> 06:24.680
To be perfectly honest...

06:45.510 --> 06:48.660
We've assembled all 60 
of our men, including myself.

07:08.190 --> 07:10.930
Men! It is time for war!

07:11.450 --> 07:14.640
The enemy are 20,000. There are 61 of us.

07:15.100 --> 07:18.120
Ahead of you lies 
a mission fraught with danger.

07:18.420 --> 07:20.700
What awaits you is a pittance of gold,

07:20.700 --> 07:24.840
pride and dignity, as well 
as gratitude from the populace.

07:25.180 --> 07:29.030
The two sides in a war insist 
that they are in the right.

07:29.030 --> 07:30.600
Both are the same.

07:30.600 --> 07:33.010
There is no justice to be found there.

07:33.010 --> 07:35.710
A frenzy to gain wealth and power.

07:35.710 --> 07:38.640
And the masses are the ones 
who always pay the price.

07:38.640 --> 07:40.760
However, this time is different!

07:40.760 --> 07:42.780
The enemy violated their pact,

07:42.780 --> 07:45.840
launching a unilateral invasion with 
their soldiers and hordes of monsters!

07:45.840 --> 07:48.620
Your mission here is to fight to defend 
the royal capital and its citizens!

07:53.410 --> 07:55.960
Let me take this moment 
to declare the following:

07:55.960 --> 07:58.790
we are undeniably 
on the side of justice here!

08:04.770 --> 08:07.670
I will step aside for about 10 minutes.

08:07.670 --> 08:12.340
If you won't take on this mission, 
use that time to take your leave.

08:12.340 --> 08:16.230
Those who remain are to then 
head off to the battlefield.

08:16.230 --> 08:18.390
I will place my hopes in your courage.

08:52.590 --> 08:55.050
All of Wolf's Fang is taking part!

08:58.510 --> 08:59.470
Embark!

09:03.140 --> 09:05.240
That was amazing, young lady.

09:05.240 --> 09:07.510
You'd make one hell of an agitator, you know.

09:07.510 --> 09:10.070
<i>The opening of that speech 
was actually stolen</i>

09:10.070 --> 09:12.490
<i>from a recruitment ad 
for Antarctic explorers...</i>

09:12.490 --> 09:13.740
<i>But still...</i>

09:13.740 --> 09:18.520
<i>None of them are prying too deeply 
into my identity or this mission...</i>

09:18.520 --> 09:21.520
<i>They make it a point not to inquire 
into their clients' private lives!</i>

09:21.520 --> 09:24.960
<i>They're professionals, 
just like Sven and his party!</i>

09:24.960 --> 09:27.900
It looks like God will be fighting 
with us for the first time in ages!

09:27.900 --> 09:28.830
God?

09:29.550 --> 09:31.430
Our guardian deity.

09:37.660 --> 09:40.720
<i>And he's brought angels with him, as well!</i>

10:01.950 --> 10:04.950
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

10:04.950 --> 10:07.950
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

10:13.250 --> 10:14.680
A message from the herald!

10:14.680 --> 10:17.470
20,000 enemy troops have arrived 
right outside the royal capital!

10:18.160 --> 10:20.160
They've formed an encampment!

10:20.590 --> 10:21.780
So they're finally here...

10:21.780 --> 10:24.830
We have less than 2,000 
soldiers left in the capital...

10:24.830 --> 10:28.100
We must hold out as long as we 
can by barricading ourselves.

10:28.100 --> 10:31.610
We can only hope that provincial 
reinforcements arrive in time.

10:36.130 --> 10:38.650
I-I-It's terrible!

10:38.650 --> 10:39.780
What's wrong?!

10:39.780 --> 10:41.490
In the courtyard...

10:41.490 --> 10:43.160
There are monsters in the courtyard!

10:43.160 --> 10:44.290
What'd you say?!

10:44.290 --> 10:45.670
Has the enemy invaded?!

10:45.670 --> 10:50.700
I believe entry into the courtyard had been 
forbidden at Miss Mitsuha's behest.

11:10.140 --> 11:12.020
Wh-What are these things?!

11:18.110 --> 11:19.950
Wolf's Fang has arrived!

11:20.650 --> 11:24.200
Zegleius Kingdom! I have returned!

11:24.880 --> 11:26.160
Miss Mitsuha!

11:26.500 --> 11:28.670
We will now proceed to move into position.

11:28.670 --> 11:31.800
And at the break of dawn, our main 
force will attack from the main gate!

11:31.800 --> 11:33.080
We'll drive the enemy back!

11:33.530 --> 11:36.050
Everyone, form a barricade 
and defend the gates!

11:36.050 --> 11:37.980
We'll lend our support, as well!

11:37.980 --> 11:38.920
Wha...

12:03.980 --> 12:05.490
Ah ah.

12:05.490 --> 12:08.340
<i>Just as we discussed, station six men each</i>

12:08.340 --> 12:10.520
<i>at the three gates other than 
the main gate to the south.</i>

12:10.520 --> 12:12.710
<i>Don't forget your designated 
weapons and ammunition.</i>

12:21.270 --> 12:22.580
Stop engines!

12:32.330 --> 12:35.270
Troops! I love this country!

12:35.270 --> 12:37.810
Aginucono adiks!

12:37.810 --> 12:39.730
<i>This country's language, huh?</i>

12:39.730 --> 12:44.320
I love this town! I love the people 
who live in this town!

12:45.860 --> 12:48.160
So I will stain these hands with blood.

12:49.420 --> 12:51.870
Wolf's Fang! Forward!

12:55.580 --> 12:57.670
Open the gate!

13:02.090 --> 13:03.660
Oh!

13:04.680 --> 13:08.510
The Messenger of Lightning goes into battle!

13:08.510 --> 13:11.010
You know who she is, old man Leiden?!

13:11.010 --> 13:14.020
Yes... I saw it with my own eyes...

13:14.450 --> 13:18.480
Just as the third princess 
was abducted in a back alley...

13:18.480 --> 13:24.190
The Messenger struck down lightning 
to save Her Royal Highness!

13:24.190 --> 13:28.160
I remember she called herself 
the Messenger of Lightning!

13:28.540 --> 13:31.870
I saw it myself through a crack in the wall!

13:31.870 --> 13:33.520
The Messenger...

13:33.520 --> 13:35.740
The Messenger of Lightning...

13:37.250 --> 13:41.230
The Messenger is taking up arms for our sake!

13:45.020 --> 13:47.090
Glory be to the Messenger!

13:49.550 --> 13:52.020
Messenger!

13:50.220 --> 13:54.060
<i>I feel like I can make out 
some unsettling words there...</i>

13:54.060 --> 13:55.460
<i>No, my ears must be playing a trick on me!</i>

13:55.460 --> 13:57.230
<i>Nope, I don't hear it!</i>

14:02.940 --> 14:05.560
<i>Mitsuha, be safe...</i>

14:23.420 --> 14:25.960
What are those? Wagons?

14:25.960 --> 14:28.570
<i>Sacrificial pawns to buy some time?</i>

14:28.570 --> 14:31.140
<i>I have no intent of playing along...</i>

14:31.140 --> 14:34.090
<i>But I suppose I'll show some courtesy.</i>

14:34.090 --> 14:37.740
Hey, negotiation time. Make it quick.

14:37.740 --> 14:38.600
Yes!

14:41.870 --> 14:44.010
Someone's coming.

14:44.010 --> 14:46.320
Snipers, take aim!

14:46.680 --> 14:49.460
Target the enemy horseback 
rider charging in!

14:49.460 --> 14:50.530
Roger.

14:52.590 --> 14:58.860
I am a nobleman of the glorious 
Alder Empire, Count Thorsten von Lotz!

14:57.540 --> 14:58.860
Aim for his right upper arm.

14:58.860 --> 15:00.650
On this occasion, our Empire—

14:59.480 --> 15:00.650
Fire!

15:01.920 --> 15:02.930
What?!

15:05.710 --> 15:10.050
Wound him intentionally so that they have to 
spare some of their men to treat him...

15:10.420 --> 15:13.760
<i>So that's what we're going for 
with the humans, young lady?</i>

15:13.760 --> 15:14.640
Yes.

15:14.640 --> 15:18.810
They don't know about guns, so it should 
cause a lot of psychological fear, as well.

15:18.810 --> 15:19.980
Roger that!

15:19.980 --> 15:21.290
All men, dismount vehicles!

15:21.290 --> 15:22.710
Prepare to engage!

15:30.780 --> 15:33.020
They attacked the negotiating envoy?!

15:33.020 --> 15:35.640
Do you barbarians have no pride or dignity?!

15:35.640 --> 15:38.360
A message for the Imperial troops who 
 have shed their pride and dignity!

15:38.360 --> 15:39.970
Wh-What'd you say?!

15:40.950 --> 15:42.670
How can we hear you from over here?!

15:42.670 --> 15:44.360
You lowly bandits joining 
forces with monsters,

15:44.360 --> 15:47.400
killing innocent civilians, 
and plundering this kingdom

15:47.860 --> 15:50.630
have no right to talk of pride or dignity!

15:50.900 --> 15:52.900
You have angered the gods.

15:52.900 --> 15:55.220
No matter how bravely you fight,

15:55.220 --> 15:58.740
you Imperial troops will 
not ascend to the heavens!

15:58.740 --> 16:01.740
You are all doomed to go to hell!

16:02.980 --> 16:06.540
Do you want to know why 
I'm so confident in saying that?

16:06.540 --> 16:09.990
You see, it's because 
that's what I've decided!

16:09.990 --> 16:12.280
Face the wrath of the gods!

16:12.800 --> 16:16.870
All light infantry and snipers, 
aim for hostile arms and legs!

16:16.870 --> 16:17.830
Fire!

16:22.310 --> 16:24.840
Wh-What in the world?!

16:25.750 --> 16:28.160
<i>Young lady, as for the monsters...</i>

16:28.730 --> 16:33.550
<i>It seems each kind is 
accompanied by one human.</i>

16:33.550 --> 16:36.300
Are they monster handlers, 
like the one from before?

16:36.760 --> 16:37.750
<i>Probably.</i>

16:38.380 --> 16:40.420
Then incapacitate them one by one.

16:44.890 --> 16:47.400
Wh... Wh... Wha...

16:47.400 --> 16:49.640
All officers in charge of monsters are down!

16:49.640 --> 16:51.900
Now the monsters won't do as we say!

16:51.900 --> 16:52.900
What?!

16:53.550 --> 16:57.060
<i>The monster regiments we established 
after much sacrifice and harsh training</i>

16:57.060 --> 16:59.580
<i>are suddenly useless?!</i>

16:59.580 --> 17:01.550
Use brute force to send in the monsters!

17:01.550 --> 17:03.450
A bit of momentum, 
and they'll go charging in!

17:03.450 --> 17:05.040
Dispatch our remaining foot soldiers, as well!

17:05.040 --> 17:07.860
Most of them are expendable peasants, anyway!

17:09.440 --> 17:10.500
Hurry up!

17:10.500 --> 17:12.900
Before they launch more of those attacks!

17:16.380 --> 17:19.710
One light round of machine 
gun fire on the monsters.

17:19.710 --> 17:23.870
Then only attack the ones who look like 
military, as well as approaching monsters.

17:23.870 --> 17:26.460
<i>Huh? Ignore the other soldiers and monsters?</i>

17:26.460 --> 17:27.230
Yep.

17:27.800 --> 17:31.850
The monsters who've lost trust and think 
they were tricked by deceitful humans...

17:31.850 --> 17:33.570
We'll send them right back to the Empire.

17:34.180 --> 17:37.860
They'll gobble up lots of enemy 
soldiers on their way back.

17:41.380 --> 17:45.670
We'll instill plenty of fear 
in the forcibly conscripted peasants,

17:45.670 --> 17:48.650
and fill them with anger 
and hatred toward the Empire.

17:48.650 --> 17:51.040
<i>Young lady, can I say one thing?</i>

17:51.040 --> 17:52.550
Yeah, what is it?

17:55.220 --> 17:56.510
You're creeping me out!

18:01.720 --> 18:03.640
Anyone who looks like they're giving orders,

18:03.640 --> 18:05.970
is wearing flashy armor, 
or is on horseback...

18:05.970 --> 18:08.240
Take all of them out completely!

18:08.920 --> 18:11.380
We were dragged here against our will!

18:11.380 --> 18:13.020
I can't take any more of this!

18:15.680 --> 18:20.370
There's no need to massacre 
the enemy troops to be victorious in war.

18:20.920 --> 18:24.160
Few wars end with most 
of the soldiers dying.

18:24.870 --> 18:27.740
In reality, they'll be done for after 
50% or so are killed in action.

18:27.740 --> 18:31.010
Usually, total defeat comes even sooner, 
once about 30% are dead.

18:31.010 --> 18:33.860
That is, they concede defeat and it's over.

18:35.810 --> 18:40.300
<i>So we'll thoroughly crush the career 
officers who are the heart of their army!</i>

18:41.540 --> 18:44.510
<i>Okay! The enemy front has begun to fall back!</i>

18:44.900 --> 18:45.970
Hmm?

18:47.220 --> 18:49.350
What... are those?

18:54.320 --> 18:56.220
The wyvern squadron is here!

18:56.220 --> 18:57.690
Now we can begin our counterattack!

18:57.690 --> 19:01.360
A triumph accomplished with 
many years and sacrifices!

19:01.360 --> 19:04.410
Strapping soldiers and wyverns, 
united by their bond

19:04.410 --> 19:07.040
to form the world's first airborne cavalry!

19:07.040 --> 19:09.200
They'll rain spears down on 
the heart of the enemy forces,

19:09.200 --> 19:11.070
and swoop down inside the gate!

19:11.070 --> 19:13.970
Then, the wyverns' powerful claws 
and bills can tear open the gate

19:13.970 --> 19:15.960
while keeping enemies at a distance,

19:15.960 --> 19:17.750
allowing their fellow troops to rush inside!

19:17.750 --> 19:18.880
It's perfect!

19:18.880 --> 19:24.100
Ah, to think I get to witness this 
monumental feat with my very own eyes!

19:24.100 --> 19:25.770
Th-This is...

19:25.770 --> 19:27.930
<i>There's no need to worry, young lady!</i>

19:27.930 --> 19:28.770
Eh?

19:28.770 --> 19:30.440
We've got God on our side!

19:39.030 --> 19:40.950
Yes, this is our God!

19:42.290 --> 19:46.860
<i>It all goes back to when we were still 
a nameless team of mercenaries.</i>

19:47.630 --> 19:49.370
<i>On that battlefield,</i>

19:49.370 --> 19:52.560
<i>we were tasked by our employer, 
the government army, with taking the rear.</i>

19:53.180 --> 19:55.130
<i>Mercenaries are expendable in the end.</i>

19:55.130 --> 19:58.690
<i>The regular army used us as decoys 
to hightail it out of there.</i>

19:59.480 --> 20:04.080
<i>After running out of guns and ammo, 
just when we thought it was the end...</i>

20:05.760 --> 20:08.260
<i>God descended upon us.</i>

20:08.930 --> 20:12.810
<i>An abandoned half-track with 
an old 20mm autocannon...</i>

20:14.130 --> 20:18.690
<i>It's thanks to this God that we 
made it through and are still alive!</i>

20:18.690 --> 20:22.480
Our fangs that tear through 
air and ground enemies alike!

20:22.480 --> 20:24.830
It's where we got our name, Wolf's Fang!

20:25.410 --> 20:26.450
Fire!

20:39.170 --> 20:40.090
Eh?

20:40.930 --> 20:43.670
I-In just a brief moment...

20:44.350 --> 20:50.460
The culmination of long years of blood, 
sweat, tears, and an immense budget...

20:50.460 --> 20:53.520
B-Blown away to pieces!

20:59.820 --> 21:02.690
<i>Well? How'd you like our God?</i>

21:02.690 --> 21:04.870
<i>I'll have to offer my prayers to him later.</i>

21:04.870 --> 21:06.570
I like the way you think.

21:06.570 --> 21:08.660
I'm sure God will be thrilled, too!

21:09.020 --> 21:10.610
<i>So, is it all over?</i>

21:10.610 --> 21:12.110
Yes, most likely.

21:25.430 --> 21:26.430
Eh...

21:28.390 --> 21:31.020
H-Hey! What the hell is that?!

22:05.920 --> 22:08.610
<i>I open my eyes, and where do I find myself?</i>

22:10.550 --> 22:13.260
<i>Maybe I should go back to bed</i>

22:15.140 --> 22:17.730
<i>Pretending I'm still half-asleep</i>

22:19.270 --> 22:23.790
<i>Running away from reality, 
to the west and east</i>

22:24.440 --> 22:26.200
<i>To be honest, life's all about</i>

22:26.200 --> 22:28.960
<i>Taking falls and getting back up 
(heavy damage)</i>

22:28.960 --> 22:32.070
<i>Hurt as it may, there's 
still a long road ahead...</i>

22:33.740 --> 22:36.530
<i>Looks like I've reached the end of my rope</i>

22:38.550 --> 22:41.040
<i>Hitting life's harder levels</i>

22:42.830 --> 22:47.400
<i>That's a test from the gods 
that I'll take on</i>

22:47.400 --> 22:49.860
<i>First things first, gotta be the economy!</i>

22:49.860 --> 22:52.510
<i>Aiming for the bourgeois life</i>

22:52.510 --> 22:54.260
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:54.260 --> 22:57.160
<i>No matter what enemies may come my way</i>

22:57.160 --> 22:59.220
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:59.220 --> 23:01.760
<i>I'll get them on my side</i>

23:01.760 --> 23:03.820
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

23:03.820 --> 23:06.360
<i>Who doesn't need money, after all?</i>

23:06.360 --> 23:11.070
<i>To the days where you need to 
scrape by one way or another</i>

23:11.070 --> 23:18.540
<i>Here's to you!</i>

24:11.970 --> 24:14.270

